## Pinned toolchain and named workflow map

`mise --version` reports `2026.7.6 macos-arm64`; `mise exec -- pnpm --version` reports `11.15.1`. Repository instructions require all commands through pinned `mise`, named workflows through `pnpm scripts run`, and no `ai-cli`. Workflow inventory was read with `mise exec -- pnpm scripts list` and metadata with `scripts show`.

- Full Glyph package gate: `mise exec -- pnpm --filter @pmndrs/glyph check`. Latest candidate receipt passes. Its component named workflows include `glyph:static-check`, `glyph:node-tests`, `glyph:shaper-tests`, `glyph:bake-check`, and `glyph:typegpu-check`; static check requires a current distribution, and shaper tests use pinned Rust/authenticated fonts.
- Native cold/prepared-query/split/rollback coverage: `glyph:shaper-tests` with the appropriate test filter. Prior specific passing receipts include `short_inter_label_assignments_use_incremental_shape_and_match_cold_output`, `sequential_measure_queries_commit_independent_existing_paragraphs`, `sequential_measurements_accept_each_edit_before_render_publication`, and `committed_measure_is_durable_and_failed_publication_delivery_discards_root`. Do not rerun without a selected candidate.
- Prepared Labs generator check: `benchmark:prepared-operations-check -- --package-root <installed Glyph root>`; deterministic only, no build/server/timing.
- Fixed seven-family acceptance: `benchmark:labs-package -- --suite full` with the repository's fixed single-call / fixed-20 policy and exact frozen candidate and saved-candidate baseline arms. Full baseline expects 145 identities; published permits two documented no-outline omissions. The handoff explicitly requires candidate, main, and published comparisons; one frozen source/archive/named-Wasm identity must bind the candidate first. Do not run now.
- Exact owned allocator memory: `benchmark:shaper-live-memory` with explicit authenticated manifest, output and frozen archive/package root. The `benchmark:application-memory-observe` workflow reports Darwin process-family physical footprint and is explicitly unsuitable for memory admission under the user's exact-owned-allocation rule.
- Browser timing diagnostic: `benchmark:dense-browser-timing` requires frozen archive SHA, Chromium and authenticated Inter Bitmap fixture; writes JSON and post-timing canvas captures. It measures CPU/render-submit and rAF timing, not GPU completion, and does not replace seven-family acceptance.
- Hero pixel check: `benchmark:editorial-hero-pixels` compares completed candidate and independent cold-main presentation receipts with externally pinned hashes; no repository source changes. Existing strict comparison retains 842 pixels differing by at most one color level, traced to prior f32 rounding; do not change tolerance.
- API/ABI and installed-consumer checks: `benchmark:packed-consumer` proves runtime baking from a frozen archive in an isolated browser consumer; `benchmark:release-comparison-check` checks exact-release Labs selection and unsafe-input rejection; `glyph:peer-check` checks declared peer floors and can add browser WebGPU verification. `glyph:node-tests` covers package/integration callers.
- Delivery sizes: `benchmark:package-size` requires built Glyph and R3F/Tres outputs plus Binaryen and can write an external report; `glyph:shaper-size-accounting` accounts for an authenticated frozen shaper. Do not refresh release snapshots.

